 "id": "turbo-html2pdf#31",
 "reason": "Paginated PDFs as Chrome 156 prints them (CSS Fragmentation \u00a75.2): the first page starts at the galley top, so page 1 keeps the leading top margins and the dissolved <html>/<body> margin/border/padding (nearly every PDF's page-1 content moves down by body's 8px margin + the first block's collapsed top margin); a forced break keeps the next block's gap; an unforced break still truncates. <html>/<body> backgrounds/borders/shadows are sliced onto every page (box-decoration-break: slice) \u2014 no corpus input decorates <html>/<body>, so that half changes no output. Attribution (napi of turbo-html2pdf consol/p5b-w2, path-patched to turbo-dom consol/p5b-w2): 5024d5c -> 41f7185 with the decoration slices disabled (margins only) = every change listed; margins-only -> 41f7185 = 0 changes. Unchanged: every layoutBoxes output (galley, not paginated), conformance-58-object-fit-cover (first block at the page top) and the surf corpora. Chrome-ward: over the 73 conformance fixtures printed by Chrome 156 page.pdf() with @page{size:A4;margin:20mm} (html2pdf's default), the first word's top on page 1 moved closer to Chrome's for 68, farther for 1 (16-position-fixed: the walker stacks the fixed box as flow content, pre-existing), the remaining ~1.8pt being font metrics. P5b-W2.",
 "control": "turbo-html2pdf crates/turbo-html2pdf-core/tests/fixtures/pagination_chrome156.json (scripts/pagination-chrome-control.mjs: Chrome for Testing 156.0.8078.4 page.pdf(), pdftoppm -r 96)",
